#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Make, check, publish and import Showcase deck bundles.

A deck bundle is a folder with a ``deck.json`` plus the files it references
(see README.md and the synthetic bundle example). This one-file CLI uses
the Python standard library only.

    showcase-deck init DIR [--title T]          scaffold a new bundle
    showcase-deck validate DIR                  check it the way the server does
    showcase-deck preview DIR                   write DIR/.preview/index.html
    showcase-deck push DIR --slug S [-m MSG]    upload changed files, publish a version
    showcase-deck versions SLUG                 list published versions
    showcase-deck pull SLUG DIR [--version N]   download a version into a folder
    showcase-deck diff SLUG A B                 compare two versions
    showcase-deck import SRC OUTDIR             convert a legacy single-file HTML deck

Environment:
    SHOWCASE_URL               base URL (default http://127.0.0.1:8000)
    SHOWCASE_AUTH_TOKEN        verified OIDC bearer token for API writes (unless behind auth proxy)
    SHOWCASE_OWNER_TOKEN       owner/workspace token; overrides the token file
    SHOWCASE_OWNER_TOKEN_FILE  token file (default ~/.config/showcase/owner-token)

The owner token is never printed, logged or put in an error message.
"""

